The file patches the real Go source of debug/elf/file.go.

The real file reads unsafe.Sizeof and unsafe.Offsetof of the 8 header types of
the ELF format. Each 1 names the layout of the format itself, and that layout
never changes. The constant block below holds the same numbers. Each other line
of the file stands as the real file writes it.

A test of the Go repository reads the same numbers again. Thus a change of the
format would break the real package first.

The real file also declares a variable of each header type. The 2 calls of the
package unsafe read that variable. The constants need no such variable, thus
each declaration goes.

